Garlic and Herb Pull Apart Bread
  --Bianca Dodson

4 c ap Flour, divided
1 packet active dry yeast (2 1/4 tsp)
3 tbsp unsalted Butter
2 tsp salt
2 tsp sugar
1 c milk
1/2 c water
8 tbsp salted butter
2 tsp Italian herb seasoning
2 cloves minced garlic
2 tbsp grated parmesan

In the bowl of the stand mixer, combine 3 c of flour, yeast, sugar, and salt. In a liquid measuring cup, warm the milk, water, and butter in the microwave in 15 s increments until just warm. Mix with the paddle attachment for 1-2 min or until the ingredients just come together, then add the remaining cup of flour. Switch to the dough hook attachment then mix for 8 min on medium speed until the dough comes together. Add the dough to a medium greased bowl and cover for 10 min. While the dough is resting, make the garlic herb seasoning for the bread. Combine melted butter, Italian seasoning, garlic cloves, and parmesan then set aside. Dump the dough onto a floured surface and cut into similar size pieces and roll into balls. Place the dough into a greased Dutch oven. Generously brush each piece of dough with the garlic herb butter sauce. Cover and let rise for an additional 45 min. Once ready to bake, brush on any additional garlic and herb seasoning. Bake for 25-30 min or until golden brown. If any additional garlic herb sauce remains, pour over the top of the bread, and serve warm. 
